ime":{"current":"10:11:53","previous":"10:17:04","deltaSeconds":-311}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":14,"finishersRank":13,"finishRateRank":94,"winningTimeRank":26,"winningTimeRankDir":18,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1966,"mensWinner":"Tommy MALONE","mensTime":"06:14:07"}},"narrative":"The 2012 Comrades Marathon was the 87th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.208 km. The race was held on Sunday, 3 June. Conditions: Cold at start. Mild to warm with scattered cloud in parts. Cool pleasant breeze early afternoon. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nLudwick MAMABOLO claimed the men's title in 05:31:03, ahead of Bongmusa MTHEMBU (05:32:42) and Leboka Noto (05:33:31). Elena NURGALIEVA won the women's race in 06:07:12, followed by Eleanor GREENWOOD (06:08:24).\n\nElena NURGALIEVA's 06:07:12 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1966 (Tommy MALONE, 06:14:07).\n\nFrom a field of 19,523 entries, 11,890 runners crossed the finish line (60.9% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 9,557 men and 2,332 women (19.6% female). The average finish time was 10:11:53.\n\nMedals awarded: 21 Gold, 19 Wally Hayward, 610 Silver, 2,022 Bill Rowan, 5,353 Bronze, 3,865 Vic Clapham. 2,774 runners (23.3%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Eric OAKER in 11:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 2010, the field was 17.0% smaller.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 55% of the finishers, with 5,323 seniors (avg 09:55:47) and 6,565 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}